    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84028" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλω-ήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλώω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sailor, seaman,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archyt.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				3.1.112
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1087
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				489a
			</span></i>; including rowers, navigators, and passengers, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1276
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				b20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1279a4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				4.3.21
			</span></i>; epith. of the Dioscuri, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				42(1).511
			</span></i> (Epid., <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>swimmer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				1.65
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Musae.
				2
			</span></i>; of fishes, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				2.196
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., <i>floating,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					23.107
				</span></i>
			.</div>
